 34AL cL E,J$from the Adopted Levels. E(level)=0.55 MeV and J|p=1+ with dominant
 34AL2cL neutron 2p1h configuration (d{-3/2}){+-1}(f{-7/2}){+2} from shell-model
 34AL3cL calculations (2012Ro25). A fit of |b decay curve in coincidence with   
 34AL4cL 3326-keV |b-delayed |g ray in {+34}Si yields a shorter T{-1/2} of 49.8 
 34AL5cL ms {I2}, which indicates that the 2+, 3326 level in {+34}Si is also fed
 34AL6cL by the |b decay of the isomer in {+34}Al. Even without decay branching 
 34AL7cL ratios, the fact that both the 0+ and 2+ levels in {+34}Si are fed by  
 34AL8cL the isomer suggests a 1+ assignment for the isomer.                    
 34AL cL T$from fit of |b decay curve in coincidence with 511-keV |g ray arising
 34AL2cL from positron annihilation. Other than the 511|g, no other |g rays are 
 34AL3cL observed in coincidence with the electron-positron pair. The second 0+ 
 34AL4cL state at 2718 keV in {+34}Si is observed to be populated by the |b     
 34AL5cL decay of the 1+ isomer in {+34}Al and to deexcite by E0 transition to  
 34AL6cL 0+ g.s. of {+34}Si via the internal pair formation (IPF). The sum      
 34AL7cL energy of the electron-positron pair is measured to be 1688 {I2}       
 34AL8cL (2012Ro25).                                                            
                                                                                
