 34SI c  2002En02: a 73-MeV {+35}Si secondary beam was produced via             
 34SI2c  fragmentation of 100-MeV/nucleon {+40}Ar primary beam on a {+9}Be      
 34SI3c  target, separated by the NSCL A1200 fragment separator, and impinged on
 34SI4c  a 93-mg/cm{+2} {+9}Be secondary target. The reaction residues were     
 34SI5c  analyzed using the S800 spectrograph. |g rays in coincidence with      
 34SI6c  scattered {+34}Si were detected using an array of 38 NaI(Tl) detectors.
 34SI7c  Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, and ({+34}Si)|g-coin. Comparisons with   
 34SI8c  shell-model calculations.                                              
 34SI c  2002En02 fits their |g spectrum using known {+34}Al |b-delayed |g rays 
 34SI2c  from 2001Nu01. 2002En02 states that an unambiguous placement of the |g 
 34SI3c  rays from 2001Nu01 is not always possible, neither is there a          
 34SI4c  one-to-one correspondence between the proposed excited states and the  
 34SI5c  shell-model calculation. A disagreement between the overall fit and the
 34SI6c  measured data is clearly visible and indicates the possibility of an   
 34SI7c  even more complex spectrum.                                            
