 34SI c  1998Ib01: {+197}Au({+34}Si,{+34}Si'|g). A 42.6-MeV/nucleon {+34}Si     
 34SI2c  secondary beam was produced by fragmentation of a 80-MeV/nucleon       
 34SI3c  {+40}Ar primary beam from the NSCL A1200 cyclotron on a 356-mg/cm{+2}  
 34SI4c  {+9}Be production target at NSCL. The reaction target was a            
 34SI5c  184-mg/cm{+2} {+197}Au. Scattered beam particles were detected using a 
 34SI6c  fast/slow plastic phoswich detector and |g rays were detected using an 
 34SI7c  array of 39 cylindrical NaI(Tl) detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, and      
 34SI8c  (scattered-{+34}Si)|g-coin. Deduced excitation cross sections and      
 34SI9c  B(E2).                                                                 
