 34P  c  2012Be11: 25 MeV {+18}O beam produced using the                        
 34P 2c  Argonne Tandem-Linac                                                   
 34P 3c  Accelerator System(ATLAS) at Argonne National Laboratory impinged on   
 34P 4c  a 260 |mg/cm{+2} thick {+18}O target enriched to 97% with Ta           
 34P 5c  backing surrounded by a nearly 4|p array of 95 CsI(Tl)                 
 34P 6c  scintillators to detect charged particles. |g-rays detected by         
 34P 7c  Gammasphere array consisting of about 100 HPGe                         
 34P 8c  detectors. Measured angular distribution, energy and intensity of      
 34P 9c  |g rays, lifetimes by DSAM. Comparison with shell-model calculations.  
 34P  d  2011BeZZ is superseded by 2012Be11                                     
 34P  c  2009Be26 (superseded by 2012Be11): E=20, 24, 25, 30, 44 MeV. Two       
 34P 2c  experiments were done:                                                 
 34P 3c  1. at FSU: E=24 and 44 MeV; detector system was an array of            
 34P 4c  6 single crystal HPGe detectors and 3 four-crystal clover detectors.   
 34P 5c  2. at LBNL: E=20, 25, 30 MeV; detector system was E-|DE Si telescope   
 34P 6c  for particles and 5 HPGe clover detectors.                             
 34P 7c  Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g, (particle)|g coin, angular distributions,     
 34P 8c  lifetimes by DSAM. Comparison with shell-model calculations.           
 34P  c  2011MaZP: E=36 MeV; beam produced using the Tandem accelerator at the  
 34P 2c  National Institute of Physics and Nuclear Engineering Bucharest;       
 34P 3c  measured T{-1/2} by |g-ray coincidence fast-timing technique using     
 34P 4c  8 HPGe detectors and 7 LaBr{-3}:Ce detectors; prompt LaBr{-3}:Ce time  
 34P 5c  resolution FWHM=470 ps {I10}; calculated reduced transition            
 34P 6c  probabilities for different M2/E3 mixing ratios and compared with      
 34P 7c  shell model estimates                                                  
 34P  c  This nuclide is of some relevance to "island of inversion"             
 34P  c  Unless noted otherwise, the data and level scheme are from 2012Be11.   
 34P  c  Relative intensities at several beam energies from 2009Be26 are given  
 34P 2c  in the table placed at the beginning of the |g ({+34}P) section.       
