 34S   H TYP=FUL$AUT=NINEL NICA, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 113, 1563 (2012)$         
 34S 2 H CUT=28-May-2012$                                                       
 34S  c  1970Mo09: {+31}P(|a,p|g) E=8.00 MeV, target of Zn{-3}P{-2} evaporated  
 34S 2c  on C foil. Used annular surface barrier Si detector for protons at 172 
 34S 3c  ' - 175|' (FWHM=90 keV for protons corresponding to the 3300 keV level 
 34S 4c  in {+34}S). Used NaI |g-ray detector at |+26|', |+40|', |+50|', |+65|',
 34S 5c  and |+90|', as well as |g-ray coaxial Ge(Li) detector at 90|', relative
 34S 6c  to the beam axis. Measured p|g, and |g-ray angular correlations. Also  
 34S 7c  studied one |g from 146 keV isomer (32 min) {+34}Cl |b{++} decay       
 34S  c  1970Gr11: {+31}P(|a,p|g) E=6-9 MeV, target of {+31}P on Au backing.    
 34S 2c  Used Ge(Li)-NaI(Tl) anti-Compton and pair escape spectrometer (annulus 
 34S 3c  of four NaI(Tl) detectors surrounding the Ge(Li)). Measured lifetimes  
 34S 4c  by DSAM at five angles between 0|' and 130|'                           
 34S  c  1970Ra17: {+31}P(|a,p|g) E=5.0-7.3 MeV, target of GaP evaporated on Ni 
 34S 2c  backing. Used Ge(Li) at 0|', 90|', and 143|' relative to the beam axis.
 34S 3c  Measured lifetimes by DSAM                                             
 34S  c  1971So01: {+31}P(|a,p|g) E=7 MeV, target of Zn{-3}P{-2} evaporated on  
 34S 2c  thick Au and Cu backings, and on thin C foil. Used Ge(Li) detector and 
 34S 3c  measured lifetimes by DSAM                                             
 34S  c  1971Mu03: {+31}P(|a,p|g) E=11.0 MeV, target of red phosphorous on C    
 34S 2c  foils. Did angular correlations by measuring |g rays with five NaI(Tl) 
 34S 3c  detectors and measured at the 8|', 30|', 45|', 60|', 90|', 120|',      
 34S 4c  270|', 315|', and 352|' angles relative to the beam axis, in           
 34S 5c  coincidence with protons stopped in an annular surface barrier detector
 34S 6c  at 180|' relative to the beam direction.                               
 34S  c  1972Jo10: {+31}P(|a,p|g) E=9.3,11.0 MeV, target of red phosphorous on C
 34S 2c  foils. Did angular correlations by measuring |g rays with five NaI(Tl) 
 34S 3c  detectors surrounding the target, in coincidence with protons stopped  
 34S 4c  in an annular surface barrier detector at 180|' relative to the beam   
 34S 5c  direction. Data at E=9.3 MeV included |gp coincidence with |g rays     
 34S 6c  recorded by Ge(Li) detector. Another experiment at E=9.3 MeV was done  
 34S 7c  with five Ge(Li) detectors surrounding the target to yield the         
 34S 8c  correlations of 5689 level whose deexciting |g rays could not be       
 34S 9c  resolved by NaI(Tl) detectors. Did spin assignments (by angular        
 34S Ac  correlations), |g-ray branching ratios, and |d values                  
 34S  c  1974Gr06: {+31}P(|a,p|g) E=7.2-8.0, 10.8, 11 MeV, target of Zn{-3}P{-2}
 34S 2c  evaporated on Ta backing. Used Ge(Li) at 0|' and 90|' relative to beam 
 34S 3c  direction. Measured p|g (annular Si surface barrier detector for       
 34S 4c  protons, Ge(Li) for |g data) and |g|g (NaI(Tl) detectors) angular      
 34S 5c  correlations. Measured lifetimes by DSAM and line shape analysis       
 34S  c  1977GrZH: {+31}P(|a,p|g) E=13.9 MeV. Measured p|g angular correlations 
 34S 2c  (with annular particle detector and three Ge(Li) for |g data) and      
 34S 3c  lifetimes by DSAM                                                      
 34S  c  1969Gr03: {+31}P(|a,p|g) E=5.90 MeV, target of Zn{-3}P{-2} evaporated  
 34S 2c  on Cu backing. Used Ge(Li) and measured lifetimes by DSAM.             
 34S  c  1970Br18: {+31}P(|a,p|g) E=4.67 MeV, target of red phosphorous on C    
 34S 2c  foils. Used two Ge(Li) detectors (planar and coaxial) and measured     
 34S 3c  lifetimes by DSAM                                                      
 34S  c  1970Cu02: {+31}P(|a,p|g) E=8.05, 8.14, 8.35 MeV, target of red         
 34S 2c  phosphorous on Ni foils. Used NaI(Tl) detectors and measured lifetimes 
 34S 3c  by DSAM                                                                
 34S  c  1971Gr26: {+31}P(|a,p|g) E=9.5 MeV, target of red phosphorous on Au    
 34S 2c  backing. Used Ge(Li) and did angular correlation and polarization      
 34S 3c  measurements for two |g rays deexciting the 5689 level                 
 34S  c  1972Gr15: {+31}P(|a,p|g) E=9.5 MeV, target of InP evaporated on Au     
 34S 2c  backing. Used Ge(Li) detector at 0|' and measured lifetimes by RDM     
 34S 3c  (recoil-distance method)                                               
 34S  c  1979Ba54: {+31}P(|a,p|g) E=6.30, 7.00 MeV. Measured linear polarization
 34S 2c  P(90|') with four Ge(Li) crystal Compton polarimeter (two different    
 34S 3c  systems)                                                               
 34S  cG $The following abbreviations are used in comments: "m" for directly    
 34S 2cG reported E|g data; "|DE{-levs}" for E|g values calculated by evaluators
 34S 3cG as energy differences of initial and final levels for reported level   
 34S 4cG energies                                                               
 34S  cG $The multipolarities from 1971Mu03 and 1972Jo10 were adopted by        
 34S 2cG evaluators based on their angular correlations measurements (A{-2},    
 34S 3cG A{-4} coefficients) and tests of spin hypotheses at 0.1% confidence    
 34S 4cG limit                                                                  
 34S  cG $Mixing ratio from 1971Mu03 and 1972Jo10 (minimum of |h{+2} as function
 34S 2cG of tan{+-1}(|d) for those spin hypotheses not rejected by the 0.1%     
 34S 3cG confidence limit criterion)                                            
 34S  cL $The energies of the levels reported by 1970Mo09 were calculated from  
 34S 2cL least-squares fit to their precisely measured and reported E|g values, 
 34S 3cL except the 4890 level for which no precisely measured |g data are      
 34S 4cL reported.                                                              
 34S  cL $The energies of the levels reported by 1970Ra17 seem to have been     
 34S 2cL measured by them at least in part. Almost all authors are common with  
 34S 3cL those of 1970Mo09, which already reported level and |g-ray energies    
 34S 4cL while in 1970Ra17 main findings are the lifetimes. However we do not   
 34S 5cL consider the level energies from 1970Ra17 because they are reported    
 34S 6cL without uncertainties (so unless we adopt some arbitrary uncertainties 
 34S 7cL we can not use these values for weighted averages). For same reason -  
 34S 8cL lack of uncertainties - we do not use neither the level and |g-ray     
 34S 9cL energies from 1971Mu03 and 1972Jo10                                    
 34S  cL $The argument "test of spin hypotheses" used for spin assignments means
 34S 2cL that several spins for the initial levels were tested by authors when  
 34S 3cL doing the fits of angular correlations                                 
 34S  cL $Spin assignments from 1977GrZH are based on their angular correlations
 34S 2cL measurements although they do not show any evidence                    
 34S  cL $Weighted averages were calculated ignoring values listed without      
 34S 2cL uncertainties                                                          
