 34S     33S(N,G) E=THERMAL            1985RA15                  ENSDF    202609
 34S   H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34S   H TYP=FUL$AUT=NINEL NICA, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 113, 1563 (2012)$         
 34S 2 H CUT=28-May-2012$                                                       
 34S  c  1985Ra15: measured E|g and I|g with a Ge detector operated in          
 34S 2c  Compton-suppressed and pair spectrometer modes at Los Alamos           
 34S 3c  Omega West reactor facility. Deduced a detailed level scheme and       
 34S 4c  compared results with data from other reactions. The                   
 34S 5c  intensities of some strong primary dipole |g rays compared with        
 34S 6c  results for similar levels populated in (d,p) data. Detailed           
 34S 7c  theoretical analysis using R-matrix approach.                          
 34S  c  Others:                                                                
 34S  c  1983Ra04: paper by the same group as 1985Ra15. Measured S(n)           
 34S 2c  for {+34}S based on 11 strong cascades. All 22 E|g values stated are   
 34S 3c  the same as in 1985Ra15.                                               
 34S  c  2007ChZX: prompt |g activation analysis (PGAA database for elemental   
 34S 2c  analysis), natural target. In the measurements at Budapest, 5 primary  
 34S 3c  and 6 secondary |g rays were identified. The energies and relative     
 34S 4c  intensities (deduced from measured elemental cross sections) are in    
 34S 5c  good agreement with those from 1985Ra15. The normalization factor      
 34S 6c  is also in agreement. The data in 1985Ra15 are much more complete and  
 34S 7c  precise, thus adopted here. For data from 2007ChZX, consult            
 34S 8c  PGAA websites at IAEA and LBNL, most of which is taken from earlier    
 34S 9c  ENSDF database which was based on data from 1985Ra15                   
 34S  c  Other: 2009KiZW (method to identify nuclear levels based on neutron    
 34S 2c  capture reactions).                                                    
 34S  cG RI$|s(mb). 1985Ra15 give cross sections in mb and quote a              
 34S 2cG multiplication factor of 0.220 to obtain intensities per 100 thermal   
 34S 3cG neutron captures                                                       
 34S  cG M,MR$From Adopted Gammas                                               
 34S  cG E(B),RI(B)$Energy from level-energy difference. Intensity is           
 34S 2cG an upper limit, deduced from Table I(x ray) of 1985Ra15                
 34S  cL E$ From least-squares fit to E|g data. Normalized |h{+2}=1.127, with   
 34S 2cL only about 10 gamma-ray energies deviating by slightly more than       
 34S 3cL two standard deviations. Doubly-placed |g rays were not used in the    
 34S 4cL fitting procedure                                                      
 34S  cL J$From Adopted Levels                                                  
 34S   N 0.220     15                                                           
 34S  cN NR$From intensity balance in the level scheme. 1985Ra15 give 0.220     
 34S 2cN with no uncertainty                                                    
