 34CL c  {+32}S+1p+1n|){+34}Cl from J|p=0+ {+32}S ground state.                 
 34CL c  1973Ca15: 9.0-MeV {+3}He beam from the Utrecht 6 MV tandem Van de      
 34CL2c  Graaff generator impinged on a natural Sb{-2}S{-3} target. Protons were
 34CL3c  detected using two Si surface-barrier detectors and |g rays were       
 34CL4c  detected using a Ge(Li) detector. Measured p|g-coin. Deduced lifetimes 
 34CL5c  using DSAM.                                                            
 34CL d                                                                         
 34CL c  1971De27: 8.0-9.0-MeV {+3}He beams from the Notre Dame model FN tandem 
 34CL2c  Van de Graaff accelerator impinged on natural CdS targets. Protons were
 34CL3c  detected using an annular Si surface-barrier detector and |g rays were 
 34CL4c  detected using NaI(Tl) detectors and coaxial Ge(Li) detectors. Measured
 34CL5c  E{-p}, E|g, I|g, and p|g(|q)-coin. Deduced levels, J, |g-ray branching 
 34CL6c  ratios, and mixing ratios.                                             
 34CL d                                                                         
 34CL c  1971Sn01: 6.8-MeV {+3}He beam from the Brookhaven National Laboratory  
 34CL2c  3.5-MeV Van de Graaff accelerator impinged on a 95% {+32}S target. |g  
 34CL3c  rays were detected using a Ge(Li) detector. Measured E|g, I|g. Deduced 
 34CL4c  levels and lifetimes using DSAM. Also measured {+31}P(|a,n|g){+34}Cl   
 34CL5c  reaction at the Stony Brook tandem Van de Graaff accelerator and       
 34CL6c  deduced lifetimes using RDM.                                           
 34CL d                                                                         
 34CL c  1970Br11: 7.5-MeV {+3}He beam from the Utrecht 6-MV tandem Van de      
 34CL2c  Graaff generator impinged on a natural ZnS target. Protons were        
 34CL3c  detected using two Si surface-barrier detectors and |g rays were       
 34CL4c  detected using a Ge(Li) detector. Measured p|g-coin. Deduced levels, J,
 34CL5c  |g-ray branching ratios, and lifetimes using DSAM.                     
 34CL d                                                                         
 34CL c  1970Br10: 5.2-MeV {+3}He beam from the Padova 5.5-MV Van de Graaff     
 34CL2c  generator impinged on a natural CdS target. Protons were detected using
 34CL3c  an annular Si surface-barrier detector and |g rays were detected using 
 34CL4c  a Ge(Li) detector and a NaI(Tl) detector. Measured E{-p}, E|g, I|g, and
 34CL5c  p|g(|q)-coin. Deduced levels, J, |g-ray branching ratios, and mixing   
 34CL6c  ratios. Also measured {+31}P(|a,n|g){+34}Cl reaction using a Ge(Li)    
 34CL7c  detector and deduced lifetimes using DSAM.                             
 34CL d                                                                         
 34CL c  1970Sy01: 5.75-MeV {+3}He beam from the University of Groningen Van de 
 34CL2c  Graaff accelerator impinged on natural ZnS target. Protons were        
 34CL3c  detected using a Si annular detector and |g rays were detected using a 
 34CL4c  NaI(Tl) detector. Measured E{-p}, E|g, I|g, and p|g(|q)-coin. Deduced  
 34CL5c  levels, J, |g-ray branching ratios, and mixing ratios.                 
 34CL d                                                                         
 34CL c  1970Th10: 9-, 9.5-, 10-MeV {+3}He beams impinged on natural ZnS target 
 34CL2c  at Nuclear Research Institute, Strasbourg, France. Protons were        
 34CL3c  detected using a Si surface-barrier detector and |g rays were detected 
 34CL4c  using a NaI detector. Measured |gp(|q). Deduced levels and J.          
 34CL d                                                                         
