 34CA c  Isotope discovery: none.                                               
 34CA c  S(2p) is negative and S(p) may be consistent with zero. {+34}Ca is a   
 34CA2c  candidate for ground-state two-proton emitter.                         
 34CA c  Theoretical calculations:                                              
 34CA c  2026Li03: S(p)=401 and S(2p)=-1987 from an average of Finite-Range     
 34CA2c  Droplet Model (FRDM12), Koura-Tachibana-Uno-Yamada (KTUY) model,       
 34CA3c  Weizsacker-Skyrme (WS4) model, and Duflo-Zuker (DZ31) model combined   
 34CA4c  with the radial basis function mirror symmetry (RBFms) approach.       
 34CA c  2024Li59: S(2p)=-1044, T{-1/2}=177.8 ns. The Q(2p) decay energy was    
 34CA2c  determined using an empirical linear relationship. The T{-1/2} was     
 34CA3c  calculated by inputting the refined decay energy into the new          
 34CA4c  Geiger-Nuttall formula.                                                
 34CA c  2024Ji17: T{-1/2}=8.1 fs from an extension of the Bayrak model with and
 34CA2c  without the deformation term. Used Q(2p)=2510 from 2021Wa16.           
 34CA c  2023Me08: T{-1/2}=64.6 ps. The WKB approximation is applied to a       
 34CA2c  Yukawa-plus-exponential model potential. Used Q(2p)=1470 from 2017Wa10 
 34CA3c  and a spectroscopic factor derived from a specific cubic-polynomial    
 34CA4c  relation.                                                              
 34CA c  2022Zo01: S(p)=259 {I96}, S(2p)=-2132 {I151}, mass excess=14497 {I98}. 
 34CA2c  Mass relations of mirror nuclei.                                       
 34CA c  2022Sa41: T{-1/2}=2.2 fs from the Coulomb and proximity potential model
 34CA2c  for deformed nuclei (CPPMDN) incorporating ground-state deformation    
 34CA3c  (|b2) and orientation effect. Used Q(2p)=2510 from 2021Wa16.           
 34CA c  2022Ro15: T{-1/2}=0.35 fs from the generalized liquid drop model       
 34CA2c  (GLDM). T{-1/2}=3.0 as from a semi-empirical analytic expression based 
 34CA3c  on a modified version of the Geiger-Nuttall law. Both calculations used
 34CA4c  Q(2p)=2510 from 2021Wa16.                                              
 34CA c  2022Pa24: T{-1/2}=0.31 ns from a two-potential approach; the nuclear   
 34CA2c  potential is obtained using the Skyrme-Hartree-Fock approach and the   
 34CA3c  Skyrme effective interaction of SLy8. Used Q(2p)=1470 from 2017Wa10.   
 34CA c  2021Xi06: T{-1/2}=3.5 fs from the Unified Fission Model (UFM),         
 34CA2c  T{-1/2}=1.7 fs from the Generalized Liquid Drop Model (GLDM),          
 34CA3c  T{-1/2}=27.5 fs from the Effective Liquid Drop Model (ELDM). These     
 34CA4c  models share a similar physical mechanism by treating the decay as a   
 34CA5c  {+2}He cluster preformed on the nuclear surface that subsequently      
 34CA6c  penetrates the Coulomb barrier. All used Q(2p)=2510 from 2021Wa16.     
 34CA c  2021Li27: T{-1/2}=79.4 ps from the Gamow-like model. Used Q(2p)=1470   
 34CA2c  from 2017Wa10.                                                         
 34CA c  2021Li16: T{-1/2}=117 ps from a two-parameter empirical formula based  
 34CA2c  on the Geiger-Nuttall law. Used Q(2p)=1470 from 2017Wa10.              
 34CA c  2020Ma35: S(p)=203 {I151}, S(2p)=-2152 {I118}, T{-1/2}=3.6 ps          
 34CA2c  {I+51-20}. Mass relations of mirror nuclei with local correlations and 
 34CA3c  a four-parameter empirical formula based on the Effective Liquid Drop  
 34CA4c  Model (ELDM).                                                          
 34CA c  2020Cu01: T{-1/2}=19.5 ps from a generalized liquid drop model (GLDM). 
 34CA2c  Used Q(2p)=1470 from 2017Wa10.                                         
 34CA c  2019Sr02: T{-1/2}=2.2 ns. A four-parameter empirical formula was fitted
 34CA2c  using the theoretical results of the Effective Liquid Drop Model       
 34CA3c  (ELDM). Used Q(2p)=1470 from 2017Wa10.                                 
 34CA c  Other decay half-life calculations: 2017Sa70, 2004Pf02, 2003Gr04,      
 34CA2c  2005Pf01, 2003Gr24, 2001Gr29                                           
 34CA c  Other structure calculations: 2005Wa15, 2005Zh28, 2002Zh09, 2001Yo12,  
 34CA2c  1998Co30, 1997Co19, 1997Pa38, 1996Sh20, 1995La03                       
 34CA c  Giant-resonance calculations: 2021Li26, 2001Sa57, 1997Ha57, 2003Ma71,  
 34CA2c  2001Sa77, 1999Sa22, 1998Ha09, 1998Ha39, 1998Sa28, 1997Ha55             
 34CA c  Experimental search:                                                   
 34CA c  A two-hour search conducted on March 27, 2012, during the 2015Su01     
 34CA2c  experiment at the Radioactive Ion Beam Line in Lanzhou (RIBLL), did not
 34CA3c  observe any events at |J200 ns that could be attributed to {+34}Ca in  
 34CA4c  the |DE-ToF spectrum.                                                  
